		{
			dependencies: ["2BEF03C52636E165"]
			description: [
				"The ME Pattern Buffer's relationship with the other hatches is &calways&r &bcompletely isolated"
				""
				"\"Recipe Cached\" is a kind of &blocked recipe&r; only when the ME Pattern Buffer matches the previously cached operating conditions (including the &bcatalyst&r, &bprogrammed circuit&r, etc.) will the machine run the recipe, and it also reduces the machine's performance cost for searching recipes"
				""
				"Supports caching multiple recipes in the same pattern (the actual recipe count must be set in the GUI of the dedicated catalyst slot)"
				""
				"In the ME Pattern Access Terminal, an ME Pattern Buffer's default name is the name of the multiblock controller it is on plus the programmed circuit setting (e.g. Super Blast Smelter-3)"
				""
				"The dedicated catalyst slot's GUI can be dragged around (there may be strange overlay display issues)"
				""
				"If the middle mouse button cannot open the dedicated catalyst slot, check whether the middle button is bound to another function that could conflict, such as inventory sorting"
				""
				"The ME Pattern Buffer forces AE to &bignore&r the &cbyproducts&r in the pattern while crafting, which can be turned off in the bottom-left corner of the GUI"
				""
				"The Copy Tool &6cannot&r copy catalyst settings; when pasting a configuration, make sure you have enough &dBlank Patterns&r in your inventory"
				""
				"The Cut Tool &6can&r carry catalyst settings"
			]
